The plural of 'dwarf' in (pre-Tolkien) English is 'dwarfs'.  'Dwarves'
and 'dwarven' are words first found in The Hobbit (iirc).  Some
fantasy authors (e.g. Terry Pratchett) have assiduously avoided using
the Tolkien plural, so I guess the alternative adjective
'dwarfish' (equally made up, I'm sure) is ingrained in my mind from
reading Discworld novels.

I suppose as Hack predates Discworld, but not Middle Earth, 'dwarves'
is probably the 'correct' one (by fantasy fiction naming convention)
for the NetHack race.

